---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import CalculatorCard from "../components/CalculatorCard.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Betting Maths: Calculators, Guides and Original Analysis"
  description="Understand the mathematics behind betting with free calculators, plain-English guides and original analysis of odds, probability, bookmaker margin, staking and market mechanics."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The mathematics behind betting markets</p>
    <h1>Understand what the numbers actually mean.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Betting Maths is an independent educational resource built around three things: useful calculators, clear explanations and original mathematical analysis. No tips, predictions or guaranteed systems—just transparent working.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="/analysis/">Explore Original Analysis</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/calculators/">Use the Calculators</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/guides/">Read the Guides</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Three ways to use Betting Maths</h2>
    <div class="pillar-grid">
      <a class="pillar-card analysis" href="/analysis/">
        <span>Investigate</span>
        <h3>Original analysis</h3>
        <p>Start with a real mathematical question and work through the assumptions, formulas, findings and limitations.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="pillar-card" href="/calculators/">
        <span>Calculate</span>
        <h3>Interactive calculators</h3>
        <p>Test odds, margins, stakes, returns, exchange liability and settlement scenarios with free tools built for the site.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="pillar-card" href="/guides/">
        <span>Understand</span>
        <h3>Plain-English guides</h3>
        <p>Learn the concepts behind the calculations, from implied probability and overround to each-way terms and hedging.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Betting Maths Analysis</p>
    <h2>Questions worth doing the maths on</h2>
    <p>Definitions are useful, but they are only the starting point. Our analysis section uses reproducible models to examine questions that are easy to overlook when looking at a headline price or promotion.</p>
    <div class="analysis-grid">
      <a class="analysis-card" href="/analysis/how-margin-compounds-in-accumulators/">
        <span>Accumulator maths</span>
        <h3>How Bookmaker Margin Compounds in Accumulators</h3>
        <p>See how receiving 95% of a fair return on each modelled leg becomes a much larger combined shortfall as the number of legs increases.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="analysis-card" href="/analysis/cash-out-fair-value/">
        <span>Cash out</span>
        <h3>What Is a Cash-Out Offer Worth?</h3>
        <p>Use a stated probability benchmark to quantify the difference between a cash-out offer and the modelled value of the remaining payout.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="analysis-card" href="/analysis/extra-places-mathematical-value/">
        <span>Each-way offers</span>
        <h3>What Does an Extra Place Actually Change?</h3>
        <p>Isolate the mathematical effect of one extra qualifying place and see why the headline number of places is only part of the offer.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/analysis/">View All Analysis</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Popular calculators</h2>
    <p>Each calculator is paired with educational context explaining what the result means, which inputs it depends on and where the calculation has limits.</p>
    <div class="grid calculator-grid">
      <CalculatorCard title="Odds Converter" description="Convert decimal, fractional and American odds and see the implied probability." href="/calculators/odds-converter/" />
      <CalculatorCard title="Overround Calculator" description="Calculate total book percentage and the margin built into a market's quoted prices." href="/calculators/overround-calculator/" />
      <CalculatorCard title="Expected Value Calculator" description="Estimate EV and expected ROI using your own probability estimate." href="/calculators/expected-value-calculator/" />
      <CalculatorCard title="Accumulator Calculator" description="Multiply several prices and see the combined odds, return and implied probability." href="/calculators/accumulator-calculator/" />
      <CalculatorCard title="Hedge Bet Calculator" description="Work through back-first and lay-first hedge stakes, liability and commission." href="/calculators/hedge-bet-calculator/" />
      <CalculatorCard title="Each-Way Calculator" description="Calculate the separate win and place parts of an each-way bet." href="/calculators/each-way-calculator/" />
    </div>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/calculators/">Browse All Calculators</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Start with the core concepts</h2>
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <a class="guide-card" href="/guides/what-is-implied-probability/"><span>Probability</span><h3>What Is Implied Probability?</h3><p>Translate a betting price into the percentage chance implied by that price.</p></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/guides/bookmaker-margin-explained/"><span>Pricing</span><h3>Bookmaker Margin Explained</h3><p>See why the implied probabilities in a market often total more than 100%.</p></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/guides/expected-value-betting/"><span>Value</span><h3>What Is Expected Value?</h3><p>Understand how possible profit and loss are weighted by a probability estimate.</p></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/guides/what-is-lay-liability/"><span>Exchange betting</span><h3>What Is Lay Liability?</h3><p>Understand why laying a selection can put more at risk than the lay stake itself.</p></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/guides/hedging-vs-cash-out/"><span>Risk</span><h3>Hedging vs Cash Out</h3><p>Compare the mechanics of a bookmaker cash-out offer with a manually calculated hedge.</p></a>
      <a class="guide-card" href="/guides/each-way-betting-terms-explained/"><span>Racing</span><h3>Each-Way Betting Terms Explained</h3><p>Separate the win and place parts and understand how the place fraction changes returns.</p></a>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/guides/">Browse All Guides</a><a class="button secondary" href="/glossary/betting-jargon-explained/">Open the Glossary</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Show the working</h2>
    <p>The site is designed around reproducible maths. Where a result depends on an assumption—such as an estimated win probability—we make that dependency explicit. Where an article uses a model rather than observed market data, we label it as a model.</p>
    <div class="standards-grid">
      <a class="standards-card" href="/methodology/"><h3>Calculation Methodology</h3><p>See the formulas, conventions, rounding approach and limitations used across the calculator library.</p></a>
      <a class="standards-card" href="/editorial-standards/"><h3>Editorial Standards</h3><p>Read how Betting Maths approaches accuracy, original analysis, sourcing, corrections and commercial independence.</p></a>
      <a class="standards-card" href="/about/"><h3>About Betting Maths</h3><p>Learn why the site exists and how calculators, guides and analysis fit together.</p></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Betting maths can explain risk. It cannot remove it.</h2>
    <p>A correct calculation does not make an uncertain event certain. Betting Maths does not tell readers what to bet on and should not be treated as a source of guaranteed income.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/responsible-gambling/">Responsible Gambling</a><a class="button secondary" href="/disclaimer/">Read the Disclaimer</a></div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .article-section { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
    .pillar-grid, .analysis-grid, .guide-grid, .standards-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
    .pillar-card, .analysis-card, .guide-card, .standards-card { display: block; padding: 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--color-bg); }
    .pillar-card:hover, .analysis-card:hover, .guide-card:hover, .standards-card:hover { border-color: rgba(31, 138, 91, 0.45); transform: translateY(-2px); }
    .pillar-card span, .analysis-card span, .guide-card span { display: inline-flex; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #eef8f3; color: var(--color-green-dark); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 800; }
    .pillar-card p, .analysis-card p, .guide-card p, .standards-card p { margin: 0; }
    .pillar-card.analysis { border-color: rgba(31, 138, 91, 0.35); background: #f4fbf7; }
    .calculator-grid { margin-top: 1rem; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .pillar-grid, .analysis-grid, .guide-grid, .standards-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  </style>
</MainLayout>
